1a1eebfd60f75da9Paul WestallIs your Family Office set up for 2027?Paul Westall on the gaps, risks and governance questions to address before you hire in 2027.

Hi Marcy

As the year comes to a close, we're launching a short podcast series in which I sat down with Sylvia Lee, who oversees our thought leadership content, to reflect on what Agreus has observed across the Family Office market in 2026.

Our aim is simple: to share practical insights that help you start 2027 strong.

Here, we look at what Family Offices should be thinking about before they hire in the new year:

• An honest review of your team: Are there gaps? Is one person carrying too much responsibility to give it the attention it needs? What happens if they're unavailable?

• Long-term risk: Do you need in-house finance or tax expertise? If you're bringing investments in-house from external managers, do you have the specialists to support that?

• Governance: Beyond the family and leadership, who provides oversight of the team and its decision-making?

